      "content": "that makes sense. so if we're looking at the 'revolutionary' side, could you give me an example of how a lesson might frame the arguments for a specific movement, like civil rights or environmentalism? i want to make sure the students see the depth and the strength of the logic used by the people pushing for change, so they aren't just seeing it as a surface-level trend.",
